  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1136 AM CDT Fri Jul 10 2026\n\nSunday through Friday:\n\nSurface high pressure and the upper ridge are expected to remain\nin place Sunday through Tuesday, with the ridge gradually\nflattening mid to late week while the surface high weakens.\nTemperatures will warm up early week under the strong upper\nridge, with highs likely cracking 90 by Monday. The warmest days\nnext week are likely to be Mon-Wed based on latest NBM probs for\nhighs greater than 90. Not out of the question to see temps push\n95 one or two days given 925 mb temps of 26-28C. Dewpoints\nshould be a bit lower than the last hot stretch though, maxing\nout in the 65-70 degree range. This should help to keep heat\nindices largely under 100 degrees. That said, plenty of \nsunshine, light winds, and heat indices in the 90s will make \nfor a hot first half of the week. \n\nAs the ridge flattens later next week, temps should fall back\ntoward normal values. Additionally, the door will open back up\nfor shower/storm chances Thursday and Friday as a shortwave or\ntwo comes over top of the flattening ridge. \n\nDDV",
